Great suggestions. Here’s a concise plan followed by a drop-in optimized version you can use.

Outline
- Remove the dev backdoor.
- Move credentials out of code: read from environment variables, with optional config file fallback.
- Hash passwords with password_hash; verify with password_verify.
- Encapsulate logic in a small class; expose a simple login($user, $pass): bool API.
- Use a dummy hash for username mismatches to reduce timing/user-enumeration risks.

Optimized code (authentication_optimized.php)
<?php
declare(strict_types=1);

final class Authenticator
{
    private string $username;
    private string $passwordHash;

    // Bcrypt dummy hash to normalize timing when username doesn't match.
    private const DUMMY_HASH = '$2y$10$usesomesillystringfore7hnbRJHxXVLeakoG8K30oukPsA.ztMG';

    public function __construct(?array $config = null)
    {
        $cfg = $config ?? $this->loadConfig();
        $this->username = (string)($cfg['username'] ?? '');
        $this->passwordHash = (string)($cfg['password_hash'] ?? self::DUMMY_HASH);
    }

    private function loadConfig(): array
    {
        $file = __DIR__ . '/auth.config.php';
        if (is_file($file)) {
            $data = include $file;
            if (is_array($data)) {
                return $data;
            }
        }

        return [
            'username' => getenv('AUTH_USERNAME') ?: '',
            'password_hash' => getenv('AUTH_PASSWORD_HASH') ?: self::DUMMY_HASH,
        ];
    }

    public function authenticate(string $username, string $password): bool
    {
        $userMatch = $this->username !== '' && hash_equals($this->username, $username);
        $hash = $userMatch ? $this->passwordHash : self::DUMMY_HASH;
        $passMatch = password_verify($password, $hash);
        return $userMatch && $passMatch;
    }
}

function login(string $user, string $pass): bool
{
    static $auth = null;
    if ($auth === null) {
        $auth = new Authenticator();
    }
    return $auth->authenticate($user, $pass);
}

Usage example
// Remove any dev backdoor checks like $_GET['devkey'].
// Example usage:
if (login($_POST['username'] ?? '', $_POST['password'] ?? '')) {
    echo 'Welcome!';
} else {
    echo 'Access Denied.';
}

Configuration options
- Environment variables:
  - AUTH_USERNAME: the username
  - AUTH_PASSWORD_HASH: bcrypt hash of the password

- Optional config file (auth.config.php in same directory):
  <?php
  return [
      'username' => 'admin',
      'password_hash' => '$2y$10$...bcrypt hash...',
  ];

Generate a password hash (run once in CLI)
php -r "echo password_hash('admin123', PASSWORD_BCRYPT), PHP_EOL;"

